  "text": "Running Blender MCP via GPT in Cursor\n\nStar_Knight12 · x · 2026-07-13\n\nThe author first tried Fable with poor results, then had Grok suggest switching to GPT. Ultimately, GPT successfully executed the task in Cursor.\n\nThey used gpt-5.6 sol to configure Blender MCP and generate a realistic floating MacBook render. Throughout the process, the author never manually opened Blender, demonstrating how such coding/creative workflows can encapsulate complex toolchains into natural language tasks.\n\nRelated event: Beginner Runs Blender Rendering via Cursor and MCP(9 posts)→\n\nOriginal post →\n\nMore from coding & agent\n\nOctopus OS: a 45k-line Rust kernel where agents rewrite their own harness mid-task — _AustinCalvert_ · 2026-10-25\n\nDev argues Rust would be better if modules, not crates, were the compilation unit — zetalyrae · 2026-10-25\n\nDev open-sources BizAgent framework where one AI lead agent manages a dozen AI employees — Low-Start2333 · 2026-10-25\n\nFormal Verification Yields to Static Analysis, Which Yields to Better Language Design — xennygrimmato_ · 2026-10-25\n\nScanning 115,798 agent ledger rows: zero capability revocations, none with expiry — Affectionate-Sun265 · 2026-10-25\n\n'Slurm's defense remains annoyingly strong': dev watches agents hit HPC wall — sloppenheimer · 2026-10-25\n\ncoding & agent channel →",
